Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:42:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 4, patch 2 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M14;
 Review 80, the SM seat's finding 37, WHICH MAIN HAS NOT CHECKED: it was made
 again before it was mended): TWO PATHS ON WHICH THE LISTENER COULD NOT LOOK
 SAY SO.

THE FINDING, MADE AGAIN. A memory that is a table and holds something that is not a number as what was read ended the listener with an error of the language, where it should exit with status 2 and say that it could not look. And a call of git that did not answer in time, while the page was looked for, was reported as "main has no page".

WHAT IS CHANGED. What the memory holds as read must be a whole number, not negative, and its record of the messages a table; otherwise the listener says that its memory cannot be read, and leaves it as it found it. A call that did not answer is said to be that. A page that is not there is still said to be not there. The old line stands in a dated note.

THE TEST plants five memories ("two", nothing, a truth value, a negative number, a record that is a list) and a git that does not answer. With the listener of the commit before, it fails on the first. 0 of 19.
